   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 237 of the laws of 2015 amending the judiciary law,\nthe civil practice law and rules and other laws relating to use of electronic\nmeans for the commencement and filing of papers in certain actions and\nproceedings, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6622",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6622-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11, Chap 237 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6622\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 237 of the laws of 2015 amending the judiciary\nlaw, the civil practice law and rules and other laws relating to use of\nelectronic means for the commencement and filing of papers in certain\nactions and proceedings, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 11 of chapter 237 of the laws of 2015 amending\nthe judiciary law, the civil practice law and rules and other laws\nrelating to use of electronic means for the commencement and filing of\npapers in certain actions and proceedings providing that sections four,\nfive, six and seven of this act shall each expire and be deemed repealed\nSeptember 1, 2022; and provided that paragraph 2-a of subdivision (b) of\nsection 2111 of the civil practice law and rules, as added by section\ntwo of this act, shall expire and be deemed repealed September 1, 2021.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis measure would extend, from September 1, 2021 to September 1, 2022,\na sunset established by Chapter 237 of the Laws of 2015 as amended by\nChapter 212 of the Laws of 2020 authorizing deployment of mandatory\ne-filing.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill, similar extenders have been passed by the Legislature the\nenactment of Chapter 237 of the Laws of 2015.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
